.TH WB\-CLEAN 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-clean \- remove the views that a session left and nothing is left in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR clean [\-\-dry\-run | \-n] [<view>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Remove the views kept on this machine for this repository that have nothing left in them: those whose session ended and that hold no commit not taken back (a commit a take\-back took is taken) and no path left uncommitted. It says first, on standard output, Removing <folder> for each view it will remove and Keeping <folder>: <what is left> for each it keeps, then removes. \-\-dry\-run (\-n) says Would remove and removes nothing. <view>, the name of the folder of a view or its whole path, as wb view \-\-kept prints it, removes that view although work is left in it, and says the work first: there is no \-\-force. A view that git could not read, or whose session runs, is never removed, named or not. It never removes the checkout, a branch or the lines of a session. Ends with 0 when it is done or there is nothing to remove, 1 when a named view is not removed, 2 when it was used wrongly or this folder is not in a git repository
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run, \-n
Say what would be removed, as Would remove <folder>, and remove nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
It is done, or there is nothing to remove.
.TP
.B 1
A named view is not removed: it is not a view kept for this repository, it was not read, its session runs, or it could not be removed.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly, or this folder is not in a git repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
